node_modules/
dist/
*.vsix
dist-test/
# Both in-host runners download somebody else's VS Code into the checkout
# root: @vscode/test-web defaults to ./.vscode-test-web, @vscode/test-electron
# to ./.vscode-test. They are caches, not sources - and they are excluded from
# the .vsix for the same reason.
.vscode-test/
.vscode-test-web/
# Anchored: the linter's icons.json is fetched into ./data at build time and
# is not ours to commit. Unanchored, this also matched src/data/ — three
# GENERATED-but-committed files (app-template, client-api, repo-dirs), each
# with a --check gate and a bump workflow keeping it in sync. They were
# tracked and ignored at the same time, which is a state nothing needs.
/data/
